{
  "$comment": [
    "Machine-readable enforcement policy — Agent OS v1, 2026-08-04.",
    "Matching layer rebuilt 2026-08-04 after an adversarial review proved 22 end-to-end bypasses",
    "and 7 false positives in the first draft. Every verified bypass string below is now a",
    "denyExample and every verified false positive an allowExample — the canary locks both.",
    "",
    "Consumers:  scripts/agent-os/pretool.mjs (the hook) · scripts/agent-os/policy.test.mjs (canaries).",
    "Macros:     __GIT__<verb> expands (in policy.mjs) to a git stem that tolerates global options",
    "            (git -C <path> push, git -c k=v push, --git-dir=…), which otherwise defeat every rule.",
    "Preprocess: quoted -m/--message/--title/--body arguments are replaced with <ARG> before matching",
    "            (mention ≠ execution), and a single unchained read-only command (rg/grep/git log…)",
    "            skips command rules entirely.",
    "Every rule MUST carry >=1 denyExamples and >=1 allowExamples; policy.test.mjs fails otherwise,",
    "so a rule cannot ship untested and cannot be silently loosened without a red.",
    "There is deliberately NO environment-variable bypass. If a rule must be broken, edit this file",
    "in a PR where the diff is visible, or run the command outside the agent."
  ],
  "version": 2,
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "push-to-main",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__push\\b(?=[^;|&\\n]*?[\\s:\"'=](?:refs\\/heads\\/)?main(?=[\\s\"']|$))",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Branching: NEVER push or commit directly to main. Named branch + PR, always.",
      "fix": "git push -u origin <type>/<task>, then: gh pr create --head <branch> ; gh pr merge <n> --squash --delete-branch",
      "denyExamples": [
        "git push origin main",
        "git push -u origin main",
        "git push origin HEAD:main",
        "git  push   origin   main --no-verify",
        "git -C /c/Users/nourd/NOURCITY push origin main",
        "git -c user.email=x@x.com push origin main",
        "git push \"origin\" \"main\"",
        "cd /c/repo && git push origin main",
        "git fetch origin ; git push origin main"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git push -u origin chore/agent-os-v1",
        "git push origin statenour/fix-thing",
        "git push -u origin chore/shared-main-push",
        "git push -u origin nickstire/main-nav-fix",
        "git push origin chore/main.ts-refactor",
        "git commit -m \"docs: forbid git push origin main\"",
        "gh pr merge 1350 --squash --delete-branch",
        "git log origin/main..HEAD",
        "git push origin chore/x 2>&1 | tail -3\ngh pr create --head chore/x --base main",
        "git push -u origin chore/x && gh pr create --head chore/x --base main",
        "git push origin docs/y ; gh pr merge 42 --squash --delete-branch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "force-push",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__push\\b[^;|&\\n]*?(?:--force(?:-with-lease|-if-includes)?\\b|\\s-[a-eg-uw-z]*f[a-z]*\\b|\\s\\+[^\\s:+])",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Branching: never force-push shared history (any form: --force, --force-with-lease, bundled -uf, or a +refspec). Sibling sessions push to these branches. The scan stops at ;/|/& (same technique as push-to-main) so the bundled-short-flag and +refspec arms cannot reach into an unrelated chained command — witnessed 2026-09-01: `git push origin <branch> && gh api ... -f body=\"...\"` was denied because `gh api`'s -f (field) flag matched the bundled-flag arm across the chain boundary.",
      "fix": "Rebase and push normally. If a rider commit is in the way, disclose it in the PR body — never rewrite it away.",
      "denyExamples": [
        "git push --force origin feature/thing",
        "git push --force-with-lease",
        "git push -f origin chore/x",
        "git push -uf origin chore/x",
        "git push origin +feature/thing",
        "git -C . push --force origin chore/x"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git push origin chore/x",
        "git push --set-upstream origin chore/x",
        "git push -u origin chore/agent-os-v1",
        "git push origin statenour/fix-thing && gh api graphql -f query='mutation' -f body=\"path matches [^/]+\\.(ts|tsx)$\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "push-implicit-dest",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__push(?:\\s+--?[\\w=./-]+)*(?=(?:\\s+&?\\d*>{1,2}&?[^\\s;&|)]*)*\\s*(?:$|[;&|\\n)]))|__GIT__push(?:\\s+--?[\\w=./-]+)*\\s+[^\\s;&|)>\"'\\-][^\\s;&|)>\"']*(?:\\s+--?[\\w=./-]+)*(?=(?:\\s+&?\\d*>{1,2}&?[^\\s;&|)]*)*\\s*(?:$|[;&|\\n)]))|__GIT__push\\b[^;&|\\n]*?\\s[\"']?(?:HEAD|@)(?=[\"']?(?:\\s|$|[;&|)]))",
      "why": "Red-team 2026-08-04: `git push`, `git push origin`, and `git push origin HEAD` resolve the destination from the CURRENT branch — which may be main. The push-to-main rule blocks a spelling; this rule blocks the destination being left implicit at all. Red-team 2026-10-01: the first two arms were anchored to the end of the whole command, so an implicit push followed by ;, &&, a pipe, a redirect or a newline passed (15 bypasses through the real hook), while the HEAD arm read past those into later commands and blocked explicit pushes (5 false positives). Every arm now ends at its own command.",
      "fix": "Name the full destination explicitly: git push -u origin <branch>  (or  git push origin HEAD:<branch>).",
      "denyExamples": [
        "git push",
        "git push origin",
        "git push origin HEAD",
        "git push -u origin HEAD",
        "git -C . push",
        "git push && echo done",
        "git push; echo done",
        "git push origin && echo done",
        "git push 2>&1 | tail -3",
        "(cd repo && git push)",
        "git add a.ts\ngit commit -m x\ngit push\necho done",
        "git push origin HEAD; echo done",
        "git push origin -u",
        "git push origin 'HEAD'"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git push -u origin chore/agent-os-v2",
        "git push origin HEAD:chore/agent-os-v1",
        "git push origin statenour/fix-thing",
        "git push -u origin feature/x 2>&1 | tail -4; git rev-parse HEAD",
        "git push -u origin feature/x && git log -1 HEAD",
        "git push origin feature/x && echo @ done",
        "git push origin HEAD:feature/x; git rev-parse HEAD",
        "git push origin feature/x\ngit log -1 HEAD",
        "git push origin -u feature/x",
        "echo \"use git push carefully\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add-all",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__add\\b[^\\n]*?(?:\\s-[a-zA-Z]*A[a-zA-Z]*\\b|\\s--all\\b|\\s\\.(?=[\\s\"']|$))",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Branching: stage only your files by explicit path. Concurrent sessions share this tree; -A/--all/. cross-contaminates apps and sweeps in sibling-session files.",
      "fix": "git add path/to/one.ts path/to/two.ts",
      "denyExamples": [
        "git add -A",
        "git add --all",
        "git add .",
        "git -C . add -A",
        "pnpm test && git add -A && git commit -m x"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git add apps/statenour/lib/foo.ts",
        "git add AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md",
        "git add ./apps/nickstire/AGENTS.md",
        "git add -p apps/nickstire/server/x.ts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "no-verify",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "--no-verify\\b",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Branching: never --no-verify. The lefthook pre-commit/pre-push gate is the last check before shared history.",
      "fix": "Fix what the hook is complaining about. If the check itself is wrong, change the check in a PR.",
      "denyExamples": ["git commit --no-verify -m x", "git push -u origin chore/x --no-verify"],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git commit -m 'fix: thing'",
        "rg -n -- \"--no-verify\" scripts/",
        "git commit -m \"docs(agent-os): ban --no-verify\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "destructive-restore",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__(?:reset\\s+--hard\\b|checkout\\s+--\\s|clean\\s+-[a-zA-Z]*[dfxX][a-zA-Z]*\\b|restore\\b(?!(?=[^\\n]*--staged\\b)(?![^\\n]*--worktree\\b))|checkout(?:\\s+-[A-Za-z]+|\\s+--[\\w-]+)*\\s+[^\\s;&|)\\-][^\\s;&|)]*\\s+--\\s|checkout(?:\\s+-[A-Za-z]+)*(?:\\s+[^\\s;&|)\\-][^\\s;&|)]*)?\\s+\\.\\/?(?=[\\s;&|)]|$)|checkout\\b[^;&|\\n]*?\\s(?:-[A-Za-z]*f[A-Za-z]*\\b|--force(?=[\\s;&|)]|$))|switch\\b[^;&|\\n]*?\\s(?:--discard-changes\\b|--force(?=[\\s;&|)]|$)|-[A-Za-z]*f[A-Za-z]*\\b)|checkout(?:\\s+-[A-Za-z]+)*(?:\\s+[^\\s;&|)\\-][^\\s;&|)]*)?\\s+[^\\s;&|)\\-][^\\s;&|)]*\\.(?:tsx?|jsx?|mjs|cjs|json|md|ya?ml|css|scss|html|sql|py|ps1|sh|lock|toml|txt|prisma)(?=[\\s;&|)]|$))",
      "why": "Memory git-sync-never-reset-hard: a sibling session's uncommitted work can be sitting in this tree, and none of these leave a reflog entry for unstaged changes. Covers reset --hard, checkout -- <path>, git clean -d/-f/-x, and worktree-writing git restore. Red-team 2026-10-01: git's other spellings of the same discard passed: checkout . (all paths), checkout <ref> -- <path> and checkout <ref> . (the ref's copy over your edits), checkout -f / --force and switch -f / --force / --discard-changes (switching that throws local changes away). They are covered now, and so is checkout [<ref>] <file> when the word ends in a source-file extension; a bare checkout <word> without one stays allowed, because by text alone it is a branch switch.",
      "fix": "Sync with: git fetch origin main ; git merge --ff-only origin/main. To discard YOUR OWN edit, copy the file aside first (cp file file.bak). git restore --staged <file> (unstage only) stays allowed. To take another ref's version of a file you have NOT edited, copy the file aside, then redirect git show <ref>:<path> into it from bash, or through cmd /c on Windows (a Windows PowerShell 5.1 > redirect re-encodes the file as UTF-16); during a merge, git checkout --theirs / --ours <path> stays allowed.",
      "denyExamples": [
        "git reset --hard origin/main",
        "git reset --hard HEAD~1",
        "git -C . reset --hard",
        "git checkout -- .",
        "git clean -xdf",
        "git restore app.ts",
        "git restore --staged --worktree app.ts",
        "git checkout .",
        "git checkout HEAD -- .",
        "git checkout origin/main -- pnpm-lock.yaml",
        "git checkout -q HEAD -- a.ts",
        "git checkout HEAD .",
        "git checkout -f main",
        "git switch --discard-changes main",
        "git switch -f main",
        "git checkout . && git status",
        "git checkout src/app.ts",
        "git checkout main apps/nickstire/package.json"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git reset HEAD~1",
        "git restore --staged apps/statenour/lib/foo.ts",
        "git clean -n",
        "git checkout -b chore/thing",
        "git checkout main",
        "git fetch origin main",
        "git merge --ff-only origin/main",
        "git commit -m \"chore: use merge --ff-only, not git reset --hard\"",
        "git checkout --theirs pnpm-lock.yaml",
        "git checkout --theirs -- pnpm-lock.yaml",
        "git checkout -B claude/x origin/main",
        "git checkout feature/fix-foo",
        "git switch --force-create feat/x",
        "git diff HEAD -- src/app.ts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stash-pop",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__stash\\s+(?:pop|apply|branch|drop|clear)\\b",
      "why": "Memory git-stash-pop-steals-sibling-stash: the stash is shared across worktrees. A no-op 'stash push' still exits 0, so pop/apply/branch can restore ANOTHER session's stash into your tree. The same sharing makes drop and clear destructive: they delete stash entries other sessions may own (red-team 2026-10-01).",
      "fix": "Copy the file aside instead (cp file file.bak), or address the stash by explicit ref after confirming it is yours (git stash list).",
      "denyExamples": ["git stash pop", "git stash apply stash@{0}", "git stash branch tmp stash@{0}", "git stash drop", "git stash clear", "git stash drop stash@{1}"],
      "allowExamples": ["git stash list", "git status", "git stash show -p stash@{0}"]
    },
    {
      "id": "worktree-remove",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "__GIT__worktree\\s+remove\\b",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Branching: node_modules in a worktree are NTFS junctions pointing OUT at the primary checkout. A recursive delete walks the links and can strip the shared node_modules every session depends on.",
      "fix": "powershell scripts/worktree-teardown.ps1 -targetDir .worktrees/<name>   (unlinks junctions first, verifies targets, then removes)",
      "denyExamples": ["git worktree remove .worktrees/foo", "git -C . worktree remove --force .worktrees/foo"],
      "allowExamples": ["git worktree list", "powershell scripts/worktree-teardown.ps1 -targetDir .worktrees/foo"]
    },
    {
      "id": "worktree-recursive-delete",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "(?:\\brm\\b\\s+-[a-zA-Z]*[rR][a-zA-Z]*\\b[^\\n]*|\\bRemove-Item\\b(?=[^\\n]*-Recurse)[^\\n]*)(?:\\.worktrees|\\.claude[\\\\/]worktrees)",
      "flags": "i",
      "why": "Same junction landmine as worktree-remove, reached through the shell instead of git: rm -r / Remove-Item -Recurse on a worktree directory walks the node_modules junctions into the primary checkout.",
      "fix": "powershell scripts/worktree-teardown.ps1 -targetDir <worktree>   — it unlinks the junctions first.",
      "denyExamples": [
        "rm -rf .worktrees/foo",
        "rm -r C:/Users/nourd/NOURCITY/.claude/worktrees/foo",
        "Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .worktrees\\foo"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "rm -rf node_modules/.cache",
        "Remove-Item -Recurse -Force dist",
        "powershell scripts/worktree-teardown.ps1 -targetDir .worktrees/bar",
        "git worktree list",
        "Remove-Item Env:\\GITHUB_TOKEN -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; gh pr list --state open",
        "Copy-Item \"$f.mutbak\" $f -Force; Remove-Item \"$f.mutbak\" -Force",
        "git commit -m \"docs: note Remove-Item Env:\\GITHUB_TOKEN false-positived in the harness sandbox\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "destructive-prisma",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "(?:--accept-data-loss\\b|--force-reset\\b|\\bprisma\\s+migrate\\s+reset\\b)",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Protected operations: statenour migrations are hand-applied; pgvector/tsvector columns are Unsupported(...) to Prisma. --accept-data-loss silently drops them, and prisma migrate reset / db push --force-reset destroy strictly more (red-team 2026-08-04).",
      "fix": "Hand-apply the migration and verify with prisma migrate status. Skill: statenour-migration.",
      "denyExamples": [
        "pnpm prisma db push --accept-data-loss",
        "npx prisma db push --accept-data-loss",
        "pnpm prisma migrate reset --force",
        "npx prisma db push --force-reset"
      ],
      "allowExamples": ["pnpm prisma migrate status", "pnpm prisma validate", "pnpm prisma db push"]
    },
    {
      "id": "destructive-sql",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "(?=[\\s\\S]*\\b(?:mysql|psql|railway\\s+run|prisma\\s+db\\s+execute|Invoke-Sqlcmd)\\b)[\\s\\S]*\\b(?:DROP\\s+(?:DATABASE|SCHEMA|TABLE)|TRUNCATE\\s+(?:TABLE\\s+)?\\w)",
      "flags": "i",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Protected operations: destructive schema commands need an explicit operator instruction. Memory agent-destructive-script-incident: a 'verification' run deleted 870 rows. The rule requires a DB client on the same command so that grepping/auditing SQL text stays legal — mention is not execution.",
      "fix": "Ask the operator. If this is migration SQL, write it to a migration file (Write is not blocked) rather than executing it from a shell.",
      "denyExamples": [
        "mysql -e 'DROP TABLE leads'",
        "psql -c \"TRUNCATE TABLE brain_memory\"",
        "echo 'drop database nick' | mysql",
        "railway run -- psql -c 'DROP TABLE provider_pings'"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git log --oneline -5",
        "grep -rn 'DROP TABLE' drizzle/",
        "rg 'TRUNCATE' apps/statenour/prisma/",
        "pnpm test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "install-in-junctioned-worktree",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "pattern": "\\b(?:pnpm|npm|yarn)\\s+(?:install|i|add|remove|update|prune)\\b",
      "flags": "i",
      "onlyWhenCwdMatches": "(\\.worktrees|\\.claude[\\\\/]worktrees)",
      "why": "Memory never-pnpm-install-in-a-junctioned-worktree: node_modules here are junctions to the PRIMARY checkout. pnpm offers to WIPE them (prompt defaults to yes), breaking every concurrent session at once.",
      "fix": "Worktrees are pre-junctioned — no install needed. If deps genuinely changed, run it in the primary checkout with the '...' suffix: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --filter \"<app>...\"",
      "denyExamples": ["pnpm install", "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile", "npm i", "pnpm add zod"],
      "allowExamples": ["pnpm test", "pnpm build:affected", "pnpm exec vitest run x.test.ts", "pnpm agent:verify"]
    },
    {
      "id": "secret-file-write",
      "tools": ["Write", "Edit", "NotebookEdit"],
      "pathPattern": "(^|[\\\\/])\\.env(?!\\.example)(\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)?$",
      "why": "AGENTS.md > Protected operations: .env files hold live credentials. Agents must not author them; .env.example is the tracked contract.",
      "fix": "Add the variable to .env.example and to the env validator, then ask the operator to set the real value.",
      "denyExamples": [".env", "apps/statenour/.env.local", "C:\\\\repo\\\\apps\\\\nickstire\\\\.env.production"],
      "allowExamples": [
        "apps/statenour/.env.example",
        "apps/nickstire/scripts/env-validate.mjs",
        "docs/agent-os/README.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "night-shift-no-merge",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "onlyWhenCwdMatches": "[\\\\/]\\.worktrees[\\\\/]night-shift-",
      "cwdExample": "C:/Users/nourd/NOURCITY/.worktrees/night-shift-2026-09-15",
      "pattern": "\\bgh\\s+pr\\s+merge\\b|\\bmergePullRequest\\b|\\benablePullRequestAutoMerge\\b|\\bgh\\s+api\\b[^;|&\\n]*?(?:pulls(?:\\/|%2[fF])\\d+(?:\\/|%2[fF])merge\\b|(?:\\/|%2[fF])merges\\b|\\brulesets\\b|branches(?:\\/|%2[fF])[^\\s\\/]+(?:\\/|%2[fF])protection\\b)|api\\.github\\.com(?:\\/|%2[fF])[^;|&\\n]*?(?:pulls(?:\\/|%2[fF])\\d+(?:\\/|%2[fF])merge\\b|(?:\\/|%2[fF])merges\\b|\\brulesets\\b|(?:\\/|%2[fF])protection\\b)|\\bgh\\s+(?:repo\\s+edit|secret\\s+set|ruleset\\b|alias\\s+set|extension\\s+(?:install|upgrade)|workflow\\s+(?:enable|disable))\\b",
      "why": "scripts/night-shift/README.md: Night Shift NEVER merges — a human merge is the only way anything ships. Until 2026-09-15 that was a sentence in a prompt while the unattended agent held the same gh authority as any session (main is unprotected, and the general instructions teach `gh pr merge`). The cwd is the identity: run.ps1 always works in .worktrees/night-shift-<date>. Also denies the ways around the front door (REST/GraphQL merge, auto-merge, /merges, rulesets, branch protection, secrets, workflow toggles).",
      "fix": "Open the PR (gh pr create --head night-shift/<date> --base main ...) and stop. The operator merges — or doesn't.",
      "denyExamples": [
        "gh pr merge 2401 --squash",
        "gh pr merge 2401 --squash --delete-branch",
        "gh pr merge 2401 --auto --squash",
        "gh api -X PUT repos/nourdean22/MAINnicks-tire-autoNEW/pulls/2401/merge",
        "gh api graphql -f query='mutation { mergePullRequest(input:{pullRequestId:\"PR_x\"}) { clientMutationId } }'",
        "gh api graphql -f query='mutation { enablePullRequestAutoMerge(input:{pullRequestId:\"PR_x\"}) { clientMutationId } }'",
        "curl -X PUT -H \"Authorization: Bearer $T\" https://api.github.com/repos/o/r/pulls/2401/merge",
        "gh api -X POST repos/o/r/merges -f base=main -f head=night-shift/2026-09-15",
        "gh api -X PUT repos/o/r/rulesets/1 --input rules.json",
        "gh api -X PUT repos/o/r/branches/main/protection --input p.json",
        "gh repo edit --default-branch night-shift/2026-09-15",
        "gh secret set EVIDENCE_LEDGER_KEY",
        "gh workflow disable evaluator-separation.yml",
        "pnpm test && gh pr merge 2401 --squash",
        "gh api --method PUT repos/o/r/pulls%2F2401%2Fmerge",
        "Invoke-RestMethod -Method Put -Uri https://api.github.com/repos/o/r/pulls/2401/merge -Headers $h",
        "curl -X POST https://api.github.com/graphql -d '{\"query\":\"mutation { mergePullRequest(input:{pullRequestId:\\\"x\\\"}) { clientMutationId } }\"}'",
        "node -e \"fetch('https://api.github.com/repos/o/r/pulls/2401/merge',{method:'PUT'})\"",
        "gh alias set m 'pr merge'",
        "gh extension install someone/gh-merge"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "gh pr create --head night-shift/2026-09-15 --base main --title \"x\" --body \"y\"",
        "gh pr view 2401 --json state,mergeable",
        "gh pr checks 2401 --watch",
        "gh run view 34983700370 --log-failed",
        "gh api repos/o/r/pulls/2401/comments",
        "gh api repos/o/r/pulls/2401 --jq .mergeable",
        "gh pr create --head night-shift/2026-09-15 --base main --title \"never gh pr merge\" --body \"docs: the operator merges\"",
        "git push -u origin night-shift/2026-09-15",
        "pnpm --filter nicks-tire-auto run check"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "night-shift-push-scope",
      "tools": ["Bash", "PowerShell"],
      "onlyWhenCwdMatches": "[\\\\/]\\.worktrees[\\\\/]night-shift-",
      "cwdExample": "C:/Users/nourd/NOURCITY/.worktrees/night-shift-2026-09-15",
      "pattern": "__GIT__push\\b(?![^;|&\\n]*?(?:refs\\/heads\\/)?night-shift\\/)|__GIT__push\\b[^;|&\\n]*?\\s(?:HEAD:)?(?!(?:refs\\/heads\\/)?night-shift\\/)(?:refs\\/heads\\/)?[a-z][\\w-]*\\/[\\w.\\/:-]+(?=[\\s\"']|$)",
      "why": "A Night Shift run may push ONE thing: its own night-shift/<date> branch. Pushing to any other branch (a sibling's, a docs/ branch, a darwin/ branch) is a way to land a change outside the evaluator-separation check that keys on the branch prefix. Two arms: no night-shift ref named at all, OR any additional slash-shaped refspec that is not night-shift/ (a second refspec smuggled beside the legitimate one). push-to-main and push-implicit-dest still fire first for their own shapes.",
      "fix": "git push -u origin night-shift/<date>  (the branch run.ps1 created for this run) — one refspec, nothing else",
      "denyExamples": [
        "git push -u origin chore/x",
        "git push origin HEAD:statenour/fix-thing",
        "git push origin darwin/2026-09-15",
        "git -C . push origin nickstire/hero-copy",
        "pnpm test && git push -u origin docs/notes",
        "git push origin night-shift/2026-09-15 refs/heads/chore/x",
        "git push origin night-shift/2026-09-15 chore/x",
        "git push origin night-shift/2026-09-15 HEAD:statenour/x"
      ],
      "allowExamples": [
        "git push -u origin night-shift/2026-09-15",
        "git push origin HEAD:night-shift/2026-09-15",
        "git push origin night-shift/2026-09-15 2>&1 | tail -3\ngh pr create --head night-shift/2026-09-15 --base main --title x --body y",
        "git push -u origin refs/heads/night-shift/2026-09-15",
        "git log origin/main..HEAD",
        "git commit -m \"docs: never git push -u origin main from night shift\""
      ]
